{"id": "EUVD-2026-86934", "enisaUuid": "b4da9870-91c0-3019-a2be-5695acb58ad8", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nigmp: convert struct ip_sf_list to RCU\n\nCommit 23d2b94043ca (\"igmp: Add ip_mc_list lock in ip_check_mc_rcu\")\nadded spin_lock_bh(&im->lock) to ip_check_mc_rcu() to prevent a\nuse-after-free while iterating im->sources during concurrent deletions.\n\nHowever, ip_check_mc_rcu() is called from RCU read-side critical\nsections in packet receive and route lookup fast paths (e.g.\n__mkroute_output(), ip_route_input_rcu(), and __udp4_lib_rcv()).\n\nWhen igmpv3_send_cr() or igmpv3_send_report() holds &pmc->lock and\ncalls add_grec() -> igmpv3_newpack() -> ip_route_output_ports(),\nan XFRM policy matching a multicast destination triggers\nxfrm_tmpl_resolve_one() -> xfrm4_get_saddr() -> __mkroute_output() ->\nip_check_mc_rcu(). This attempts to acquire &im->lock while &pmc->lock\nis already held on the same CPU, triggering a lockdep recursive locking\nwarning / deadlock.\n\nFix this by converting IPv4 struct ip_sf_list to RCU, mirroring the\nIPv6 implementation in net/ipv6/mcast.c:\n\n1. Add struct rcu_head to struct ip_sf_list and annotate sf_next,\n   sources, and tomb as __rcu pointers.\n2. Use rcu_assign_pointer() and kfree_rcu() for list updates and\n   deletions.\n3. Remove spin_lock_bh(&im->lock) from ip_check_mc_rcu() and traverse\n   im->sources locklessly with for_each_psf_rcu(), reading and writing\n   counter fields with READ_ONCE() and WRITE_ONCE().\n\nNote: RCU conversion of /proc/net/mcfilter will be done in a\nseparate patch.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:35:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:54:31", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/01131daffc4b64f1652e23dc3e6e2f601eda781d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f5182dfad54277267a8cb0c004a9cd4cf35aeebb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d3011d1f293478c730aa0870490afa145c37600e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e3206419bdb04e2087d8cc6be324df8639b3fac5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2987ee196c88dbde0463dc87d5fb209c684e34a2"], "aliases": ["GHSA-2hrc-mwqg-6fr2", "CVE-2026-98103"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0f6023b6-cf27-306d-81ed-90462033d4ae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "78967749984cf3614de346c90f3e259ff8272735"}, {"id": "173dae1f-d799-3d64-90b2-723b5c9fe1fa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "1a3b3967-920e-38fe-98e4-5b522fc1e642", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.14.3 <5.15"}, {"id": "2a884a6d-3c46-3ac5-a583-c677aba0e29b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.19.207 <4.20"}, {"id": "321b8c43-0d20-3c2b-b819-79711471e4ef", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "23d2b94043ca8835bd1e67749020e839f396a1c2 <e3206419bdb04e2087d8cc6be324df8639b3fac5"}, {"id": "3341f375-8237-35ef-84e9-b2ead8d5d7b0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d84708451d9041dff8a81e3718f821f12d2eb6c5"}, {"id": "3e2714e7-7d6e-3657-91f8-c862f32808e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "23d2b94043ca8835bd1e67749020e839f396a1c2 <01131daffc4b64f1652e23dc3e6e2f601eda781d"}, {"id": "44a9e41b-5ae0-3fc2-8a88-7f50f7b6a2f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.4.284 <4.5"}, {"id": "584ef24a-fc7a-3cc6-895e-ee310aabc2ae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.9.283 <4.10"}, {"id": "595281e1-ea75-31c5-81ed-98aff2598e4b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d1a3c6d5925a8d00a32c5ef2d674dd9c0ce89c95"}, {"id": "63ca0652-0f16-39e1-900b-5c22d92a8f3e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "676e940c-9009-3ad7-a781-5ab0efb71ab1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4768973dffed4d0126854514335ed4fe87bec1ab"}, {"id": "6bdc3635-a42d-3fd4-b2e9-adf712126841", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.10.64 <5.11"}, {"id": "703436bc-ed56-3fae-bedd-e3e5754b8041", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15"}, {"id": "74118df1-219a-3206-bcc2-aa09ab2d6b68", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ddd7e8b7b84836c584a284b98ca9bd7a348a0558"}, {"id": "8263ac60-1219-39a5-9a06-63bcc1a503ad", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b24065948ae6c48c9e20891f8cfe9850f1d748be"}, {"id": "a5f4ee2f-e1f7-3acf-b2f1-c6c17b022dc3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "961447ff60291b91e27d5c32fa549c1411ad3b70"}, {"id": "b031141f-5a11-3e29-9b41-ea0fa46bc652", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "23d2b94043ca8835bd1e67749020e839f396a1c2 <d3011d1f293478c730aa0870490afa145c37600e"}, {"id": "b42d9658-219a-3109-94f9-b730f4aa537f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "d68da16f-a73e-36c2-80ce-731df88d32f5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "d96232f9-1baa-3ac5-b65b-053366ca7e1f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.4.145 <5.5"}, {"id": "d994f5e2-4901-31cc-8b59-acb8560097f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "dfbf18f7-de8f-3161-b49a-7a558ac0616b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.13.16 <5.14"}, {"id": "eb81dd83-df43-3812-8a06-44d07ef5732f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}